  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "**Original comment by xiota (Bitbucket: [xiota](https://bitbucket.org/xiota), GitHub: [xiota](https://github.com/xiota)).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThe `PROC_TARGET_NUMBER` option appears to override existing `-march` settings in `CXXFLAGS`.  According to [x86 Options](https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/x86-Options.html), `-march` produces instructions that may not run on other processors.  Building without setting `PROC_TARGET_NUMBER` allows options already set in `CXXFLAGS` to be used.\n\nThank you for your help figuring this out.\n",
